Prefer a specific root filesystem by UUID.

Both SYSTEM and USERDATA can carry the pmOS_root label (the flat install
labels SYSTEM; moving the rootfs to the 12.6 GiB USERDATA partition creates
a second one). Look the UUID up first and fall back to the label.

--- a/init_functions.sh
+++ b/init_functions.sh
@@ find_root_partition() {
 	# mount_subpartitions() must get executed before calling
 	# find_root_partition(), so partitions from b) also get found.
+	# Prefer the USERDATA rootfs by UUID; SYSTEM may still carry the same
+	# pmOS_root label.
+	if [ -z "$PMOS_ROOT" ]; then
+		PMOS_ROOT="$(find_partition "e1a93fd5-2e76-4cf8-b775-47f6a165f683" "" "" "")"
+	fi
 	if [ -z "$PMOS_ROOT" ]; then
 		PMOS_ROOT="$(find_partition "$root_uuid" "$root_path" "pmOS_root" "TYPE=crypto_LUKS")"
 	fi
